# Project Structure Template

Purpose:
  Defines the AI-readable project structure under
  .sdd/projects/{project_name}/project/. Every module, component,
  API, and data model is declared here with clear ownership.

Owns: ./

Structure:
  README.md:
    purpose: Human-readable project overview
    format: Markdown
    template: README.template.md

  inbox/:
    purpose: Flat user input storage — any file name is accepted
    format: any
    rule: no custom folder structure — flat files only

  modules/:
    purpose: Business logic modules
    format: module.sdd per bounded context

  components/:
    purpose: Reusable UI/logic components
    format: component.sdd per component

  api/:
    purpose: External API contracts
    format: api.sdd per endpoint group

  data/:
    purpose: Data models and schemas
    format: schema.sdd per aggregate

  docs/:
    purpose: Human-readable documentation
    format: Markdown
    mirror: .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/

Rules:
  [PRJ1] Every module MUST have an owner.
  [PRJ2] Every component MUST be mapped to a module.
  [PRJ3] Every API MUST reference a module.
  [PRJ4] Every data model MUST reference an aggregate.
  [PRJ5] project/ is AI-readable, docs/ is human-readable.
  [PRJ6] project/ and docs/ MUST have 1:1 mapping.
  [PRJ7] Every change MUST be recorded in git with rationale.
  [PRJ8] Commit messages MUST follow: what changed, why, impact.
  [PRJ9] inbox/ is flat storage — no subdirectories or custom structure.
  [PRJ10] prompts/ folder MUST NOT exist in project root.

Navigation:
  Modules: @modules/
  Components: @components/
  API: @api/
  Data: @data/
  Docs: @../docs/

State: +
